{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Naphtali, sated with favor.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it means he is sated with the favor of the Holy One, blessed be He, in the manner mentioned above, ״ורצון שוכני סנה״; and he shall be filled with the blessing of YHWH, and inherit sea and south, and this alludes to his inheritance, which is to the southwest." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״נפתלי שבע רצון הממלא ברכת ה'״ — that is זאת, as it says ״וזאת הברכה״. ״ים ודרום״ — the World to Come is likened to the sea (Job 11:9) ״ורחבה מן ים״; this world to the south, as it says (Joshua 15:19) ״כי ארץ הנגב נתתני״. And this is what they expounded in Sefer ha-Bahir: ״ים ודרום ירשה״ — it should have said ירש (he inherited); rather, ים ודרום יהי רש — everything is given to you, if only you would keep His ways." "<b>And according to</b> my opinion, the hint in all this is shalom and the berit, and even ḥokhmah and binah are רש; and this is what it says: ים ודרום יהי רש." "<b>And know</b> that Naphtali and Asher encamp with Dan in the north, and their banner was the eagle, and this is inscribed in the letters נ'פתלי ש'בע ר'צון, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:24.734086997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}